    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d807">

                <pb facs="0881" n="793" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg793"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCormick to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-10-07"><hi rendition="#italic">October 7,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 193.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit to you
                    herewith a copy and translation of a note received from Count Lamsdorff,
                    imperial minister for foreign affairs, in reply to mine of August 22 last,
                    relating to the resolution adopted by the House of Representatives of the United
                    States on April 21 last, concerning “the freedom of travel and sojourn in
                    Russia, without regard to race, creed, or religious faith,” of all American
                    citizens, which was transmitted to me in your dispatch No. 127, of July 1
                    last.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert S.
                    McCormick.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d807-a1.xml" xpointer="d807-a1"/>
